From dc529d33597138fcd0d7719bf0f1009ff2c4dc93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Barattolo <barattolo@barattolo.store>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:26:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fee: read the seller's fee by the pair of trade keys, and
 stop asking again at bond lock

Patch 0005 keeps one side row per order, rewritten at every take attempt;
under the anti-abuse bond several attempts race on one order, and patch
0008 re-ran the discount lookup at lock to put the winner's row back. Two
holes: a lookup that fails at lock (server restarting, breaker open)
writes a full-fee row while order.fee keeps the discounted snapshot from
the bond, so the seller's fee falls back to the buyer's; and a rival take
whose lookup was still in flight writes its row after the winner's lock.

Every attempt now writes its fees under its pair of trade keys
(barattolo_fees_takes) and the seller's fee is read by the pair the order
carries (seller_fee_of; show_hold_invoice passes the keys, the order does
not carry them yet there). At lock nothing is asked again and nothing is
written: one journal line with the numbers the trade runs on.
---
 src/app/bond/flow.rs |  17 ++--
 src/barattolo_fee.rs | 224 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 src/util.rs          |  10 +-
 3 files changed, 232 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

